  # ============================================================
  # ABOUT
  # ============================================================
  - block: markdown
    id: overview
    content:
      title: About Me
      subtitle: ''
      text: |-
        I am a Biomedical Engineer, **Magna Cum Laude**, and an M.Sc. candidate
        in Biomedical Engineering at **Universidad de los Andes**, where I work
        with the Biomedical Computer Vision (BCV) Group under the supervision of
        [Prof. Pablo Arbeláez](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=k0nZO90AAAAJ).

        My research focuses on **artificial intelligence for biomedical applications**,
        with particular interests in multimodal learning, computer vision,
        foundation models, representation learning, and spatial transcriptomics.

        My work spans medical imaging, histopathology, spatial gene-expression
        prediction, echocardiography, and multimodal biomedical data analysis.

        In parallel, I am completing an undergraduate degree in **Instrumental Music
        — Piano** at Universidad Nacional de Colombia, where I have developed a
        strong background as a classical pianist.
    design:
      columns: '1'


