  # ============================================================
  # RESEARCH EXPERIENCE
  # ============================================================
  - block: markdown
    id: experience
    content:
      title: Research Experience
      subtitle: ''
      text: |-

        ### Graduate Research Assistant
        **Biomedical Computer Vision Group (BCV), Universidad de los Andes**  
        *Aug. 2024 — Present*

        Working on artificial intelligence for biomedical applications across
        medical image computing, multimodal learning, foundation models, and
        spatial transcriptomics.

        **Spatial Gene-Expression Prediction**  
        Developing multimodal and representation-learning methods for predicting
        spatial gene expression from histopathology across heterogeneous spatial
        transcriptomics datasets.

        **EchoRisk-MICCAI — Echocardiography Foundation Models**  
        Led a four-researcher team developing a foundation-model-based solution
        for cardiac risk prediction from echocardiography. Adapted Echo-Vision-FM
        and EchoCLIP through fine-tuning, multi-view modeling, ensembling, and
        test-time augmentation.

        **HyCLoST / SpaRED — Spatial Transcriptomics**  
        Contributed to standardized and reproducible benchmarking across 26
        spatial transcriptomics datasets, including experimental design,
        benchmarking, results analysis, manuscript preparation, and technical
        restructuring.

        **CARDIUM — Multimodal Prenatal Diagnosis**  
        Contributed to a multimodal prenatal diagnostic dataset, structured
        maternal clinical variables, and multimodal fusion between clinical and
        visual representations.

        ---

        ### Junior Researcher
        **Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation — Orquídeas Program**  
        *Jul. 2026 — Present*

        Working on AI-based biodiversity monitoring, including camera-trap image
        curation, species-classification models, and integration of computational
        tools for ecological data analysis.
    design:
      columns: '1'


